        'Yes, twin pregnancies are monitored more closely than single-baby pregnancies, and how often depends on whether your twins share one placenta or have separate ones. Twins sharing a placenta (monochorionic) are typically scanned every 2 weeks from 16 weeks onward; twins with separate placentas (dichorionic) usually have their anomaly scan around 20 weeks, then scans every 4 weeks after that.',
