        'Twins sharing a placenta carry a specific risk called twin-to-twin transfusion syndrome, where blood flow between the babies becomes unbalanced; catching this early makes a real difference, which is why monochorionic twins are scanned more often. Even without this specific risk, twin pregnancies are watched more closely overall since growth patterns between the two babies need comparing at each visit.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.forYou, '', [
        'Confirm with your doctor early on whether your twins share a placenta, since this determines your entire monitoring schedule going forward. Expect more appointments than a single-baby pregnancy, which, while it can feel like a lot, is simply proportionate, careful attention to two growing babies rather than a sign anything is wrong.',
