        'From around 20 weeks onward, lying flat on your back can make you feel dizzy, lightheaded, or nauseous, since your growing womb presses on a major vein carrying blood back to your heart. This is called supine hypotension, and it\'s easily fixed by simply turning onto your side.',
      ], []),
