        'Yes, mild vision changes are common in pregnancy, usually blurriness or dry, irritated eyes, caused by fluid retention and hormonal shifts affecting your cornea and tear production. These changes are typically temporary and resolve after delivery or once breastfeeding ends.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.why, '', [
        'Pregnancy hormones and fluid retention can thicken and change the curvature of your cornea, the clear front surface of your eye, which affects how light focuses and can make contact lenses feel less comfortable. The same hormonal shifts can also reduce tear production, leading to dry, scratchy, or occasionally watery eyes.',
