  PregFaq(
    id: 'PREG-BABY-015',
    number: 185,
    month: 4,
    question: 'What does the placenta actually do?',
    category: 'Baby Development',
    applicability: 'All trimesters',
    canI: 'Not applicable',
    sensitivity: 'No',
    parts: [
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.direct, '', [
        'The placenta is a temporary organ, unique to pregnancy, that delivers oxygen and nutrients to your baby, removes waste, produces the hormones that sustain your pregnancy, and shields your baby from many infections and harmful substances in your blood. It\'s genuinely one of the most remarkable organs your body ever builds, entirely from scratch, then lets go of at delivery.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.why, '', [
        'Your blood and your baby\'s blood never actually mix; a thin barrier inside the placenta lets oxygen, nutrients, and antibodies pass through while keeping the two blood supplies separate. This same barrier acts as a selective filter, letting beneficial things through while blocking many harmful ones, though it isn\'t a perfect shield against everything.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.forYou, '', [
        'Everything you eat, drink, or take genuinely does reach your baby through this pathway, which is exactly why nutrition, avoiding harmful substances, and following your doctor\'s medication guidance matter throughout pregnancy. The placenta\'s position and health are also why conditions like placenta previa or a low-lying placenta get monitored so closely.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.doctor, '', [
        'Your placenta\'s position and function are checked at your routine scans; ask your doctor if you\'d like more detail on what your specific scan showed.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.perspective, '', [
        'It\'s easy to overlook the placenta amid everything else pregnancy brings, but it is quite literally doing the work of your baby\'s lungs, kidneys, and digestive system, all at once, for nine months.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.takeaways, '', [], [
        'Delivers oxygen and nutrients, and removes waste.',
        'Produces hormones that sustain your pregnancy.',
        'Acts as a selective filter, though not a perfect one.',
        'Your blood and your baby\'s blood never actually mix.',
        'Its position and health are why some scans focus closely on it.',
      ]),
    ],
    related: [
      'PREG-HEALTH-029',
      'PREG-BABY-017',
      'PREG-BABY-016',
    ],
  ),
  PregFaq(
    id: 'PREG-BABY-016',
