    sensitivity: 'Yes',
    parts: [
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.direct, '', [
        'You\'re entitled to the same maternity leave, medical care, and government scheme support as any other pregnant woman in India, and Indian law specifically protects your right to be your child\'s sole legal guardian without needing to name the father. Support exists, both practical and emotional, and reaching for it is a sign of strength, not something to feel you must manage entirely alone.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.whyMatters, '', [
        'A landmark Supreme Court ruling confirmed that an unmarried mother can register her child under her own name alone, without disclosing the father\'s identity, and this right has been consistently upheld since. Government maternity schemes and the Maternity Benefit Act apply to you exactly as they would to anyone else; your marital status doesn\'t change your entitlements.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.forYou, '', [
        'Build a support network deliberately, whether that\'s family, close friends, or other single mothers, since practical help in the early weeks after delivery matters enormously and doesn\'t have to come from a partner specifically. If you ever feel unsafe, isolated, or need support, the national Women Helpline (181) and One Stop Centres (Sakhi Centres) offer medical, legal, and emotional support under one roof.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.doctor, '', [
        'Tell your doctor you\'re navigating this alone so they can factor that into your care and support planning; there\'s no need to explain your circumstances beyond what you\'re comfortable sharing.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.perspective, '', [
        'Doing this without a partner changes the shape of your support system, not its importance; building one deliberately is simply part of the plan, not a sign anything is missing.',
